      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For those of us with x670e chipset motherboards, SOMEBODY HAS FOUND A FIX and for me at least, it works! It appears to be an issue with Easy Anti-Cheat and certain hardware.\n\nhttps://rog-forum.asus.com/t5/amd-600-series/x670e-usb4-and-easyanticheat-cause-stuttering/td-p/980441\n\n1. Go to the Windows power plan settings by pressing the Windows key and typing \"edit power plan\"\n\n2. Click \"Change advanced power settings\"\n\n3. Go to USB Settings -> USB selective suspend settings -> set to \"Disabled\"",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
