      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}: I would like to make a last comment about this bug. I forgot this page existed and I fixed this issue a few days ago at long last.\n\nI thought it could be beneficial to whom may be interested in fixing that issue.\n\nFirst, it's important to note my spec:\n\nAMD Ryzen 9 7950x\n\nMSI GeForce RTX 3090 VENTUS 3X 24G OC\n\nGigabyte B650 AORUS ELITE AX ATX AM5\n\n64GB of Ram (1x ADATA XPG LANCER RGB 32 GB + 1x the same but none RGB Variant)\n\nAnd also important to note the exact issue I was having:\n\nI would launch the game, then whenever I am in a world, alone or not or even simply on the logging screen, every time at exactly 5 minute mark, the game would completely freeze my whole PC. (Important to note: I have tried to launch the game without EAC, which I know won't let me go pass the logging screen, and after 5 minutes, it did NOT freeze my PC.)\n\nOnce the PC freeze, multiple situation could occur:\n\n- The PC could bluescreen with error \"CLOCK_WATCHDOG_TIMEOUT\", which happens when a too long desync hapenned between the CPU instructions and the CPU can't continue.\n\n- The PC would just go Black screen without a BSOD and the restarts never comes. In some rare cases the restart did happened.\n\n- The PC unfreeze after about 10 seconds or so of freezing up. This might either make you able to continue playing as if nothing happened for as long as you want now OR it might have the effect of Crashing SteamVR still if you are in VR. Which will close VRChat if it happens.\n\nIn order to fully debug the issues here is all the things I did or considered:\n\n- I bought a new SSD Crucial T700 2TB + installed brand new Windows 11.\n\n- Updated Windows 11 + all drivers to latest version.\n\n- Unplugged everything else from the PC, beside mouse and keyboard. Including the GPU at one point to rule it out.\n\n- I ran a memtest on all my 64GB of ram (took 7h lol) and my ram was 100% fine.\n\n- I tried playing around with some bios setting proposed here and there on internet, virtualisation, TPM and more.\n\n- I installed ONLY Steam, SteamVR and VRChat on the system and nothing else.\n\n- I even tried the pinned solution about power management of USB.\n\n- I bought a CPU replacement for my Ryzen 9 7950x.\n\n- I bought and installed a new Motherboard \" MSI MAG X670E TOMAHAWK WIFI ATX \" + A brand new PSU of 1200W instead of 1000W.\n\nThis last step of switching the motherboard and PSU was what actually fixed my issue. My theory like mentioned above is that there seems to be some instability issues with B650 motherboard OR the fact that some motherboard weren't shipped out when the 7950x existed yet and altho a BIOS update made it compatible I suspect the motherboard to not be 100% stable with such CPU. This or the Motherboard I had, the B650, may have been faulty?\n\nImportant to note tho that I have NEVER faced any other repetitive bluescreen or similiar issues with other games, software, etc. Only VRChat.\n\nI would hope that either Motherboard manufacturer find a solution for this OR EAC dig a bit more into this issue. I'll even be happy to provide my Motherboard for testing so they could figure it out, who knows.\n\nSo yeah, in conclusion, one might have to go all the way to replace their motherboard in order to fix that bluescreen issue mentioned above with the same symptoms.\n\nI hope this may be useful for anyone. Thank you for reading.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
