  "details": "1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Wait\n\nAfter about 5 minutes from the time that I launch the application, my entire PC is brought to a crawl for around 20-30 seconds. The slowdown affects my entire computer. The issue seems to be worsened when VRChat’s window has focus. “System” CPU usage in Task Manager spikes up to about 20% during this period. This happens on both the live build and the Open Beta, and in both Desktop and VR modes.\n\nLogs:\n\nLive [1359] Desktop: https://pastebin.com/e48PvhZK\n\nBeta [1370] Desktop: https://pastebin.com/58Yw5Mip\n\nVideos:\n\nVideo example of the bug on Desktop on the Open Beta: https://youtu.be/O8SsZkHexHc\n\nVideo example of the bug on the live build with Task Manager open: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6TDExD3Wnic\n\nNo other application or game on the PC causes this behavior. It is limited only to VRChat.\n\nEdited as it also occurs on the 1360 build that was released about an hour or so after I made this post",
